# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore - restrictive Docker build-context filter (QA finding F-P6-H)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deny-by-default posture: EVERYTHING is excluded from the build context first,
# then ONLY the paths the multi-stage Dockerfile actually COPYs are re-included
# (.mvn, mvnw, pom.xml, src). Anything new added to the repository is therefore
# excluded from the image build unless it is explicitly re-included below.
#
# WHY (what this keeps OUT of the build context and image layers):
#   * secrets / local config  - .env, *.env, docker-compose.yml (never in a layer)
#   * the large legacy/ COBOL reference tree (hundreds of files; not built)
#   * target/ host build output, .git/ history, docs/, diagrams/, blitzy-deck/,
#     blitzy/ scratch, and .github/ CI config - none are needed to build the jar
# This shrinks and speeds the build context, removes an accidental-secret-leak
# vector, and keeps image layers minimal. The Dockerfile builds the jar purely
# from .mvn + mvnw + pom.xml + src, so nothing else belongs in the context.
# =============================================================================

# --- Exclude everything by default (most restrictive) ------------------------
*

# --- Re-include EXACTLY what the Dockerfile needs ----------------------------
!.mvn
!mvnw
!pom.xml
!src

# --- Defense in depth: drop noise even inside the re-included trees ----------
# Host build output must never leak in (target/ is top-level and already excluded
# by `*`, but guard against any nested occurrence under a re-included path).
**/target
# Compiled artifacts.
**/*.class
# Any environment/secret file accidentally placed under a re-included path.
**/*.env
# Editor/OS cruft.
**/.DS_Store
**/*.iml
# Ad-hoc validation scratch files must never enter an image.
**/blitzy_adhoc_test_*
